WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Imagine traveling to a country where you don't speak the language.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.060
When you need directions, shouting the one word you know louder and louder doesn't

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:08.840
help you communicate.

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.940
It just confuses and upsets the people around you.

5
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.080
For decades, traditional medicine has relied on a similar approach.

6
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.360
Using synthetic chemicals, we try to forcefully switch a single biological target on or off,

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.340
hoping to command the body to heal.

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.400
But human biology is a connected web.

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:33.400
When a drug forces one part to react, surrounding parts break down, creating severe side effects.

10
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.740
Because of this blunt approach, many therapies struggle.

11
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.640
Clinical data shows common medications help anywhere from 1 in 25 to 1 in 4 people.

12
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.600
To genuinely heal tissue and resolve disease, we have to stop trying to force the body

13
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.240
into submission.

14
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.060
We need to learn how to speak its native language.

15
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.100
That native language is written in proteins.

16
00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.040
We call this Instructional Medicine, an approach that uses the body's own natural signaling

17
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.200
proteins to coordinate healing instead of forcing a reaction.

18
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.240
Think of these proteins like a piece of paper folding into a delicate origami swan.

19
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.040
The biological instructions they carry are entirely dependent on their complex, fragile,

20
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.060
three-dimensional shape.

21
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:17.980
Here is the challenge.

22
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.600
The traditional manufacturing processes used for most medicines rely on intense heat and

23
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.620
harsh chemical treatments.

24
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.440
Applying those harsh methods to these sensitive proteins is like slamming a heavy press down

25
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.940
onto that origami swan.

26
00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:37.820
Once the three-dimensional structure unfolds, the therapeutic message is permanently destroyed.

27
00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:44.560
To successfully use natural proteins as medicine, we need a completely different kind of assembly

28
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:44.820
line.

29
00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:50.620
We need a system that protects this biological signal from the moment it is discovered to

30
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.480
the exact second a patient receives it.

31
00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.300
Instructional Biology has built exactly that.

32
00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:02.440
A five-step closed-loop platform engineered to keep these fragile proteins completely safe.

33
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.300
Step one is discovery.

34
00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:09.260
An artificial intelligence maps networks to find the exact protein instruction.

35
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:15.480
Step two, manufacturing extracts this protein in cold temperatures, keeping folds intact.

36
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.900
Step three, ultra-short laser pulses shatter pathogens without heat.

37
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.800
Step four, the protein is packed into an exosome for safe delivery.

38
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.420
Step five is feedback.

39
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:33.260
After the medicine is delivered, wearable technology monitors the patient's physical response in

40
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:33.800
real time.

41
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.540
That real-time biological data feeds right back to the artificial intelligence.

42
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.740
Every single dose helps the system learn, making the next round of discovery even more

43
00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.020
precise.

44
00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.360
This chart outlines the architecture.

45
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.000
On the left, the five steps operate as one vertically integrated chain, without handoffs

46
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.260
that could damage the instructions.

47
00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.980
On the right, the platform is modular.

48
00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:02.520
Each step operates independently, allowing partners to license specific technologies for

49
00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.120
their research.

50
00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.220
For decades, we have tried to treat illness by forcefully altering the body's chemistry.

51
00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:15.400
By mapping the body's natural signaling network, we can move away from synthetic side effects

52
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.960
and toward a harmonious way to heal.

53
00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:25.460
By protecting these delicate biological instructions at every step, Instructional Biology is building

54
00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.400
medicine made by the body, for the body.
